design/ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:40:**Motor drive and recording light (sheet 7).** MOTOR (F6) through R61 100 ohm to the gate of Q1, R62 100 kohm gate to ground, Q1 source to ground, drain MOTOR_DRV; D1 cathode on VDD_3V0, anode on MOTOR_DRV. M1 is on the band sheet. Light (W5): VDD_3V0, R41 680 ohm, LED1, drain of Q2; Q2 source to ground, gate on VDD_MIC. No chip pin touches the light.
design/ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:67:- Q1, Q2 (G, S, D pad numbers), LED1 (anode, cathode), M1 (plus, minus and tail contact numbers: VC0720B088L has an FPC tail, no polarity printed), BT1 (tabs), X1, X2.
design/ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:119:Checks kept: section 7 pin plan (now with the three A5 spare rows), contact pad order, R41 and the light, P3.05 spare, designators, every pin once, single-pin nets, rails of section 3, H8, KiCad export compare. Checks removed or changed: (a) the check that each JOY line passes the wire link J2, wire, J3 (J2, J3, W5 to W10 no longer exist; A5-3 and A5-9 replace it); (b) the LR check on U5 to U8 became a SELECT check on U5, U6 (same logic); (c) the second-level R33, R34 data check and the FUNC rows for U7, U8, SW1 five-way pins and EVPAVAA1A (parts removed; A5-1, A5-3, A5-5 replace them). `prove_fail.sh` (A3 proofs) still holds the PWR_FLAG ERC probe; its first case names a pin LR that no longer exists and its output is the A3 state.
design/ecad/ring/sch-notes.md:172:Fixed in the owned files: K1 (motor angle: `bom.csv` line 44 no longer says -38; its place waits for the rebuild, 17.11), K2 (the record pill is gone, line 40), K3 (joystick: line 78 and line 75 carry no +38), K4 (BT1: line 50 and `parts.csv` line 41 say 15 to 20 mAh and 28.4 mm), K5 (pads: line 61 says inside, 17.12), K6 (protection circuit: line 51), K7 (cross radius 2.1 mm: lines 39 and 78), K8 (this file, change e), K10 (charge voltage, change f, in the owned files), K12 (section 11.4), K16 (R41 key figure: line 48 now (3.0 V - 2.0 V) / 680 ohm = 1.5 mA as W5).
